    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MRS PATMORE: It is. Daisy take the soufflés out of the oven while I find my specs.\nDAISY: This country needs a shake-up.",
      "ISOBEL: It seems rather a waste of money.\nVIOLET: Here we go.\nCORA: Isn't that what the Monarchy's for? To brighten the lives of the Nation with stateliness and glamour?\nISOBEL: To quote Tennyson, \"Kind hearts are more than coronets, And simple faith than Norman blood.\"",
      "DAISY: Not you too. I am disappointed.\nMRS PATMORE: Ignore her.",
      "DAISY: I won't be waiting on any valets and lady's maids, thank you very much.\nANNA: Before we get hot under the collar, let's just wait and see what they have to say.",
      "CORA: This is nice. Princess Mary wants us for tea tomorrow at Harewood.\nMARY: I've got so much to do.\nCORA: I wonder if that means the young couple have taken over the big house?"
    ]
  },
